#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Makes the Art Loft ready for Pinterest: product markup, readable print addresses, specific titles and descriptions, the medium line, alt text, the heading contrast fix and the Pinterest claim tag setting. Brings four older test expectations up to date. The new tests are only put in place if every edit succeeds. It does not open the site to search engines and does not touch the database.

Run it from the project folder, AFTER unzipping starscapes-pinterest-ready-24oct.zip into it:   python3 tools/add-pinterest-ready.py

What it does: it makes exact edits to 14 files and, only if all succeed, puts six new tests in place.
  scripts/dynamicPages.mjs, scripts/make-share-pages.mjs, scripts/shareHead.mjs, src/artloft/AdminPrints.jsx, src/artloft/ArtLoftScene.jsx, src/artloft/PrintCard.jsx, src/artloft/PrintPage.jsx, src/artloft/artLoftApi.js, src/artloft/artloft.css, src/data/siteSettings.js, src/rooms/postit.css, test/dynamic-pages-build.test.js, test/dynamic-pages.test.js, test/share-head.test.js

How it keeps you safe:
  - It checks ALL 14 files first. If any is not exactly the way it expects, it changes NOTHING and says which.
  - Before changing a file it keeps a copy, ending .before-pinterest-ready.
  - It is safe to run twice: a file already done is left alone.
  - The new files (INSTALL-PINTEREST.txt, tools/pinterest-files/test_art-loft-heading-contrast.test.js.staged, tools/pinterest-files/test_print-address-api.test.js.staged, tools/pinterest-files/test_print-address-pages.test.jsx.staged, tools/pinterest-files/test_print-pages-build.test.js.staged, tools/pinterest-files/test_print-pages-pinterest.test.js.staged, tools/pinterest-files/test_print-redirects.test.js.staged) come in the zip itself.
"""
